-- arm P: a PYTHON GUI application (meld) --------------------------
  ok    arm P: the closure fetched completely          = yes
        arm P closure: 136 store paths — nothing about the
           LIBRARIES failed. The defect is downstream of the closure.
  ok    arm P: no artefact was produced                = no
  ok    arm P: resolveEntry oscillated                 = yes
  ok    arm P: and it ended in 'no entry point'        = yes
        ⛔ THE MECHANISM, exactly: bin/meld is a makeBinaryWrapper ELF whose
           target bin/.meld-wrapped is a PYTHON SCRIPT. ReadWrapper returns
           nothing for a script and elfx.IsELF is false, so
           lastExistingStorePath scans the script's text and resolves back
           to bin/meld. Five hops, then no entry point (assemble.go:60).
        ⭐ IT IS A TOOLING GAP, which is the category T-080 is about — NOT a
           statement that nix cannot do Python.

